# README is part of the ship

`docs/` is local-only. `README.md` is what GitHub and new clones see. If you ship behavior or update product docs, update `README.md` in the same change.

At least:

- Version string and the `.deb` install example (`artek-buddy-client_<VERSION>_all.deb`)
- "What you can do today" when the user-visible story changed
- Bring-up / compose / `.env.example` when a new service or env var shipped
- Changelog already has the release notes; README states the current product, not the full history

English. Do not put Funnel hostnames, tailnet IPs, or local compose in it.
